    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194271": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant Professor - Macroeconomics Colby College: Department of Economics Location Waterville, ME Open Date Sep 24, 2026 Description We are searching for a macroeconomist with potential for excellence in research and teaching who can contribute to our macroeconomics curriculum, especially at the intermediate level. All department faculty also offer elective courses that are informed by their scholarship. The teaching load at Colby is 4.5 classes per year, typically achieved in the department through three distinct courses. We are seeking candidates from a wide variety of backgrounds who, through their teaching, scholarship, and service, will contribute to access, belonging, and inclusive teaching within the campus community. Colby is a selective liberal arts college located in Central Maine with high standards for teaching and research. Our 20 continuing department faculty have active research agendas generously supported by the College, including a pre-tenure sabbatical during the fourth year, significant start-up and continuing research funds, and department-funded student research and teaching assistants. Qualifications Our review of completed applications will begin on November 13, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. We plan to conduct first-round interviews in mid-December and to schedule campus visits for finalists in January. To be considered for an interview, your application dossier must include: (i) a cover letter that describes your motivation for applying to Colby and outlines your research agenda; (ii) your curriculum vitae; (iii) three confidential letters of recommendation; (iv) a representative sample of your research; (v) your graduate transcript; (vi) a statement of teaching philosophy that demonstrates a commitment to undergraduate teaching in a liberal arts environment; (vii) and evidence of classroom teaching effectiveness, including course evaluations if available. Candidates should have completed a Ph.D. prior to September 1, 2027.  The anticipated salary range for this position is $119,800 to $123,800, commensurate with rank, experience, qualifications, and other relevant factors. Application Instructions Please submit all materials electronically to: https://apply.interfolio.com/194271 Please direct any questions about the position to: econsearch@colby.edu Please visit www.colby.edu and http://www.colby.edu/economics/ for more information about the College and Department of Economics. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Colby is a private, coeducational liberal arts college that admits students and makes personnel decisions on the basis of the individual’s qualifications to contribute to Colby’s educational objectives and institutional needs. The principle of not discriminating on the basis of race, color, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, caste, national or ethnic origin, marital status, genetic information, political beliefs, veteran or military status, parental status, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, physical or mental disability unrelated to the job or course of study requirements is consistent with the mission of a liberal arts college and the law. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze,